Bloody, hell. What's the Minister of Magic doing here?

272
00:28:10,810 --> 00:28:12,650
To what do we owe the pleasure, Minister?

273
00:28:12,700 --> 00:28:16,640
I think we both know the answer to that question, Mr. Potter.

274
00:28:24,970 --> 00:28:26,400
This is?

275
00:28:34,850 --> 00:28:35,540
Herein it is set forth,

276
00:28:35,540 --> 00:28:38,930
the last will and testament of,

277
00:28:38,980 --> 00:28:43,540
Albus Percival Wulfric Brian Dumbledore.

278
00:28:43,870 --> 00:28:48,240
"First, to Ronald Billius Weasley,

279
00:28:48,390 --> 00:28:50,920
I leave my deluminlator. "

280
00:28:51,780 --> 00:28:54,180
"A device, of my own making,

281
00:28:54,230 --> 00:28:59,210
In the hope, that when things seem most dark...

282
00:29:01,230 --> 00:29:02,990
It will show him the light. "

283
00:29:09,900 --> 00:29:12,330
- Dumbledore left this for me? - Yeah.

284
00:29:13,870 --> 00:29:15,040
Brilliant.

285
00:29:16,960 --> 00:29:17,930
- What is it? - Open it.

286
00:29:30,620 --> 00:29:31,700
Wicked.

287
00:29:34,580 --> 00:29:37,610
"To Hermione Jean Granger,

288
00:29:37,660 --> 00:29:42,660
I leave my copy of 'The Tales of Beedle the Bard'."

289
00:29:43,050 --> 00:29:47,390
"In the hope that she find it entertaining and instructive "

290
00:29:48,410 --> 00:29:49,800
My mom used to read me those.

291
00:29:50,950 --> 00:29:52,550
The wizard and the hopping pot,

292
00:29:52,550 --> 00:29:54,570
Babbity Rabbity and the Cackling Stump.

293
00:29:57,130 --> 00:29:59,630
Come on. Babbity Rabbity.

294
00:30:00,830 --> 00:30:01,970
No?

295
00:30:03,060 --> 00:30:04,770
"To Harry James Potter

296
00:30:06,320 --> 00:30:07,870
I leave the snitch he caught

297
00:30:07,870 --> 00:30:09,020
"in his first

298
00:30:09,020 --> 00:30:10,180
Quidditch match at Hogwarts.

299
00:30:10,230 --> 00:30:14,600
As a reminder of the rewards of perseverance...

300
00:30:17,470 --> 00:30:18,550
and skill. "

301
00:30:39,650 --> 00:30:40,670
Is that it then?

302
00:30:41,150 --> 00:30:42,290
Not quite.

303
00:30:42,910 --> 00:30:45,020
Dumbledore left you,

304
00:30:45,330 --> 00:30:47,460
a second bequest.

305
00:30:48,610 --> 00:30:51,610
The sword of Godric Gryffindor.

306
00:30:53,270 --> 00:30:54,670
Unfortunately, the sword of Gryffindor

307
00:30:54,670 --> 00:30:57,020
was not Dumbledore's to give away.

308
00:30:58,190 --> 00:31:01,090
As an important historical artifact it belongs...

309
00:31:01,140 --> 00:31:02,180
to Harry.

310
00:31:03,060 --> 00:31:04,750
It belongs to Harry.

311
00:31:05,190 --> 00:31:06,830
It came to him when he most needed it

312
00:31:06,830 --> 00:31:07,410
in the Chamber of Secrets.

313
00:31:07,460 --> 00:31:09,160
The sword may present itself

314
00:31:09,190 --> 00:31:11,110
to any worthy Gryffindor, Miss Granger,

315
00:31:11,160 --> 00:31:13,510
that does not make it that wizards property.

316
00:31:14,870 --> 00:31:15,810
And in any event,

317
00:31:15,850 --> 00:31:18,480
the current whereabouts of the sword are unknown.

318
00:31:18,530 --> 00:31:19,760
Excuse me?

319
00:31:19,810 --> 00:31:21,200
The Sword is Missing.

320
00:31:22,690 --> 00:31:25,990
I don't know what you are up, to, Mr. Potter,

321
00:31:26,370 --> 00:31:29,630
but you can't fight this war on your own.

322
00:31:30,410 --> 00:31:32,360
He's too strong.

323
00:32:34,050 --> 00:32:35,560
Hello, Harry.

324
00:32:36,270 --> 00:32:38,460
I've interrupted your deep thoughts, haven't I?

325
00:32:38,510 --> 00:32:40,220
I see it growing small in your eyes.

326
00:32:40,260 --> 00:32:41,950
Of course not. How are you, Luna?

327
00:32:41,980 --> 00:32:42,680
Very well,

328
00:32:42,780 --> 00:32:45,020
I've been bitten by garden a gnome and numbed my thumb.

329
00:32:45,060 --> 00:32:47,170
Gnome saliva is very beneficial.

330
00:32:47,440 --> 00:32:48,730
Xenophilius Lovegood.

331
00:32:48,780 --> 00:32:49,710
We live just over the heel.

332
00:32:49,900 --> 00:32:50,830
Nice to meet you, sir.

333
00:32:51,540 --> 00:32:52,680
I trust you know Mr. Potter that we at the Quibbler,

334
00:32:52,720 --> 00:32:54,940
disagree with the Daily Prophet,

335
00:32:54,940 --> 00:32:58,070
and have always fully supported Dumbledore...

336
00:32:58,110 --> 00:33:02,210
during his lifetime and in his death, support you just as fully.

337
00:33:03,540 --> 00:33:04,530
Thank you.

338
00:33:05,180 --> 00:33:08,130
Come Daddy. Harry doesn't want to talk to us right now.

339
00:33:08,170 --> 00:33:09,710
He's just too polite to say so.

340
00:33:16,310 --> 00:33:17,680
Excuse me, sir.

341
00:33:17,720 --> 00:33:19,300
- May I sit down? - Mr. Potter.

342
00:33:19,690 --> 00:33:22,140
By all means, here.

343
00:33:26,020 --> 00:33:28,300
I found what you wrote in the Daily Prophet,

344
