really moving.

345
00:33:29,500 --> 00:33:32,580
You obviously knew Dumbledore well.

346
00:33:33,220 --> 00:33:35,110
Well, I certainly knew him the longest.

347
00:33:35,160 --> 00:33:38,270
Unless we don't count his brother Aberforth,

348
00:33:38,340 --> 00:33:41,340
and somehow people never do seem to count, Aberforth.

349
00:33:42,600 --> 00:33:44,230
I didn't even know he had a brother.

350
00:33:45,490 --> 00:33:47,860
Dumbledore was always very private, even as a boy.

351
00:33:47,910 --> 00:33:50,100
Do not despair, Elphias.

352
00:33:50,150 --> 00:33:54,520
I'm told he's been thoroughly unrevealed by Rita Skeeter.

353
00:33:54,570 --> 00:33:57,850
In 800 pages.

354
00:33:58,280 --> 00:33:59,530
Word has it

355
00:33:59,740 --> 00:34:02,130
that someone talked to her.

356
00:34:02,800 --> 00:34:05,670
Someone who knew the Dumbledore family well.

357
00:34:06,160 --> 00:34:09,380
Both you and I know who that is, Elphias.

358
00:34:09,430 --> 00:34:11,540
A monstrous betrayal.

359
00:34:12,790 --> 00:34:15,040
Who are, who are we talking about?

360
00:34:16,280 --> 00:34:18,290
Bathilda Bagshot.

361
00:34:19,930 --> 00:34:20,580
Who?

362
00:34:20,660 --> 00:34:22,440
My god, boy. She is only the most...

363
00:34:22,450 --> 00:34:25,860
celebrated magical historian of the last century.

364
00:34:27,700 --> 00:34:31,630
She was as close to the Dumbledore's as anyone.

365
00:34:32,260 --> 00:34:33,960
Oh, I'm sure Rita Skeeter

366
00:34:33,960 --> 00:34:37,250
thought it well worth a trip to Godric's Hollow,

367
00:34:37,300 --> 00:34:40,650
to take a peek into that old bird's records cage.

368
00:34:40,700 --> 00:34:41,970
Godric's Hollow?

369
00:34:43,180 --> 00:34:45,320
Bathilda Bagshot lives in Godric's Hallow?

370
00:34:45,370 --> 00:34:47,600
That's where she first met, Dumbledore.

371
00:34:47,650 --> 00:34:49,150
You don't mean to say he lived there too.

372
00:34:49,200 --> 00:34:50,830
The family moved there

373
00:34:50,880 --> 00:34:53,670
after his father killed those three Muggles.

374
00:34:53,720 --> 00:34:56,070
It was quite the scandal.

375
00:34:57,030 --> 00:34:59,290
Honestly my boy,

376
00:34:59,340 --> 00:35:01,880
are you sure you knew him at all?

377
00:35:28,440 --> 00:35:31,300
Ministry has fallen.

378
00:35:32,150 --> 00:35:35,900
Minister of Magic, is dead.

379
00:35:38,180 --> 00:35:40,030
They are coming.

380
00:35:40,620 --> 00:35:42,460
They are coming.

381
00:35:49,350 --> 00:35:51,150
Nice meeting you, Mr. Potter.

382
00:36:02,230 --> 00:36:03,470
Ginny!

383
00:36:03,700 --> 00:36:05,890
Go! Go!

384
00:36:23,320 --> 00:36:24,570
Where are we?

385
00:36:24,620 --> 00:36:26,100
Shaftesbury Avenue.

386
00:36:26,150 --> 00:36:28,340
I used to come up here to theaters with mom and dad.

387
00:36:29,980 --> 00:36:32,320
I don't know why I thought of it. It just popped into my head.

388
00:36:33,180 --> 00:36:34,010
This way.

389
00:36:38,810 --> 00:36:40,370
We need to change.

390
00:36:46,810 --> 00:36:47,810
Bloody Hell

391
00:36:47,810 --> 00:36:52,810
- Undetectable Extension charm. - You're amazing, you are.

392
00:36:53,610 --> 00:36:55,340
Always a total surprise.

393
00:36:57,010 --> 00:36:59,340
Ah, that'll be the books.

394
00:37:05,980 --> 00:37:08,150
What about all the people at the wedding?

395
00:37:08,150 --> 00:37:09,000
Do you think that we should go back?

396
00:37:09,050 --> 00:37:10,100
They're after you, mate.

397
00:37:10,390 --> 00:37:12,150
We'd put everyone in danger by going back.

398
00:37:14,660 --> 00:37:17,690
- Ron's right. - Coffee

399
00:37:18,770 --> 00:37:21,110
- A cappuccino please - You?

400
00:37:22,720 --> 00:37:25,240
- What she said. - Same.

401
00:37:28,980 --> 00:37:32,370
So where do we go from here? Leaky Cauldron.

402
00:37:33,600 --> 00:37:35,000
It's too dangerous.

403
00:37:35,560 --> 00:37:37,220
If Voldemort has taken over the Ministry,

404
00:37:37,310 --> 00:37:38,750
none of the old places are safe.

405
00:37:38,790 --> 00:37:42,010
Everyone from the wedding would have gone underground, into hiding.

406
00:37:42,060 --> 00:37:44,920
My rucksack with all my things. I've left it at the burrow.

407
00:37:50,140 --> 00:37:53,910
You're joking.

408
00:37:53,910 --> 00:37:57,360
I had the essentials, packed for days. Just in case.

409
00:37:58,140 --> 00:38:00,440
By the way, why're the jeans not my favourite?

410
00:38:01,370 --> 00:38:02,170
Down!

411
00:38:03,280 --> 00:38:04,230
Stupify!

412
00:38:20,600 --> 00:38:21,780
Petrificus Totalus!

413
00:38:26,450 --> 00:38:28,950
Go! Leave.

414
00:38:33,670 --> 00:38:35,870
Lock the door, get the lights.

415
00:38:46,190 --> 00:38:47,300
This one's names Rawl.

416
00:38:48,350 --> 00:38:50,600
He was on the astronomy tower the last night they killed Dumbledore.

417
00:38:52,270 --> 00:38:53,430
This is Dolohov.

418
00:38:54,210 --> 00:38:56,060
I recognize him from the wanted notice.

419
00:38:57,880 --> 00:38:59,880
So what we're gonna do with you, eh?

420
00:39:01,000 --> 00:39:02,480
Kill us if it was turned round, wouldn't you?

421
00:39:02,480 --> 00:39:04,410
We kill them, they'll know we were here.

422
00:39:04,460 --> 00:39:09,810
- Ron. - Suppose he did Mad-eye? How would you feel then?

423
00:39:12,280 --> 00:39:15,500
It's better we wipe their memories.

424
00:39:15,500 --> 00:39:21,130
You're the boss. Hermione.

425
00:39:21,130 --> 00:39:22,870
You're the best with spells.

426
