The question is he didn't actually destroy the real Horcrux.

458
00:44:11,390 --> 00:44:13,920
Spying on us, have you.

459
00:44:13,970 --> 00:44:18,720
Kreacher, has been watching.

460
00:44:18,770 --> 00:44:20,410
Maybe he knows where the real locket is?

461
00:44:23,710 --> 00:44:26,930
Have you ever seen this before? Kreacher?

462
00:44:27,660 --> 00:44:33,420
- It is Master Regulus's locket! - There were two, weren't there?

463
00:44:34,600 --> 00:44:36,060
Where's the other one?

464
00:44:38,720 --> 00:44:42,850
Kreacher doesn't know, about the other locket.

465
00:44:42,900 --> 00:44:45,860
Yes, but did you ever see it? It was in this house.

466
00:44:45,910 --> 00:44:50,170
Filthy mudblood that's what you are, Blood traitor Weasley!

467
00:44:50,220 --> 00:44:51,700
Answer her.

468
00:44:53,900 --> 00:44:55,070
Yes.

469
00:44:57,180 --> 00:44:58,290
It was here,

470
00:44:59,350 --> 00:45:00,820
in this house.

471
00:45:01,860 --> 00:45:03,900
Most evil object.

472
00:45:04,370 --> 00:45:05,880
How do you mean?

473
00:45:05,880 --> 00:45:11,470
Before Master Regulus died, he ordered Kreacher to destroy,

474
00:45:11,510 --> 00:45:15,550
but no matter how hard Kreacher tried, he could not do it.

475
00:45:15,550 --> 00:45:18,350
Well, where is it now?

476
00:45:18,400 --> 00:45:23,210
- Did someone take it? - He came in the night.

477
00:45:23,260 --> 00:45:29,080
He took many things including the locket.

478
00:45:30,380 --> 00:45:31,840
Who did? Who was it, Kreacher?

479
00:45:34,490 --> 00:45:36,440
Mundungus.

480
00:45:37,380 --> 00:45:40,380
Mundungus Fletcher.

481
00:45:41,990 --> 00:45:43,360
Find him.

482
00:46:05,080 --> 00:46:06,880
My father will hear about this.

483
00:46:11,870 --> 00:46:16,060
Hey losers. He isn't here.

484
00:46:29,350 --> 00:46:32,110
As your new Minister for Magic,

485
00:46:32,870 --> 00:46:37,310
I promise to restore this temple of tolerance

486
00:46:38,510 --> 00:46:39,870
to its former glory.

487
00:46:41,200 --> 00:46:42,920
Therefore beginning today,

488
00:46:44,200 --> 00:46:46,910
each employee will submit themselves,

489
00:46:48,310 --> 00:46:49,760
for evaluation.

490
00:46:51,610 --> 00:46:55,080
But know this, you have nothing to fear,

491
00:46:56,160 --> 00:46:58,310
if you have nothing to hide.

492
00:47:54,340 --> 00:47:55,330
They have flesh memories.

493
00:47:58,740 --> 00:48:00,450
When Scrimgeour first gave it to you,

494
00:48:01,170 --> 00:48:03,370
I thought, it might open at to your touch.

495
00:48:04,930 --> 00:48:07,610
That Dumbledore hidden something inside it.

496
00:48:18,140 --> 00:48:22,530
Harry Potter, how long it's been!

497
00:48:24,580 --> 00:48:25,630
Get off me!

498
00:48:33,480 --> 00:48:34,630
Expelliarmus!

499
00:48:35,460 --> 00:48:36,800
What you playing at?

500
00:48:36,850 --> 00:48:38,880
Setting a pair of bleeding house elves after me?

501
00:48:38,930 --> 00:48:40,680
Dobby was only trying to help.

502
00:48:40,940 --> 00:48:43,380
When Dobby saw Kreacher in Diagon Alley,

503
00:48:43,510 --> 00:48:45,370
Which Dobby thought was curious.

504
00:48:45,530 --> 00:48:49,970
And then Dobby heard Kreacher mention Harry Potter's name.

505
00:48:50,020 --> 00:48:54,190
And then Dobby saw Kreacher talking with the thief.

506
00:48:54,240 --> 00:48:57,090
Not a thief? You foul little...

507
00:48:57,820 --> 00:48:58,650
git.

508
00:48:59,370 --> 00:49:03,620
I'm a purveyor of rare and wondrous objects.

509
00:49:03,640 --> 00:49:05,400
You're a thief, Dung, everyone knows it.

510
00:49:05,490 --> 00:49:10,050
- Master Weasley, so good to see you. - Like your shoes.

511
00:49:11,760 --> 00:49:14,060
Listen, I panicked that night, alright?

512
00:49:16,340 --> 00:49:18,680
Can't help it if Mad-Eye fell off his broom.

513
00:49:20,510 --> 00:49:21,730
- You. - Tell the truth.

514
00:49:21,760 --> 00:49:23,120
When you turned this place over,

515
00:49:23,350 --> 00:49:24,140
don't deny it,

516
00:49:25,290 --> 00:49:26,680
you found a locket, am I right?

517
00:49:26,680 --> 00:49:28,810
Why, was it valuable?

518
00:49:29,030 --> 00:49:32,340
- So, was it? - He's worried he didn't get enough money for it.

519
00:49:32,910 --> 00:49:34,690
Bleeding give it away, didn't I?

520
00:49:35,410 --> 00:49:38,730
There I was plogging my wares in Diagon alley,

521
00:49:39,250 --> 00:49:42,200
when some Ministry hag comes up and asks to see me license.

522
00:49:43,200 --> 00:49:44,970
Says she the one would lock me up.

523
00:49:45,790 --> 00:49:49,250
Would have done too, if she hadn't taken a fancy to that locket.

524
00:49:49,370 --> 00:49:51,660
Who was it? The witch, do you know her?

525
00:49:51,710 --> 00:49:52,940
Know her?

526
00:49:58,140 --> 00:50:00,900
She's there. Look.

527
00:50:03,620 --> 00:50:05,500
Bleedin' bone who.

528
00:50:46,960 --> 00:50:50,390
Right, remember what we said.

529
00:50:50,900 --> 00:50:54,220
Don't speak to anyone, unless absolutely necessary.

530
00:50:54,870 --> 00:50:57,160
Just, try and act normal.

531
00:50:57,210 --> 00:50:59,720
Do what everybody else is doing.

532
00:51:00,280 --> 00:51:02,870
If we do that and with a bit of luck we'll get inside.

533
00:51:03,810 --> 00:51:05,180
- And then... - It gets really tricky.

534
00:51:05,230 --> 00:51:06,890
Correct.

535
00:51:07,420 --> 00:51:10,410
- This is completely mental. - Completely.

536
00:51:10,460 --> 00:51:13,690
The world's mental. Come on.

537
00:51:14,690 --> 00:51:16,330
We have a Horcrux to find.

538
00:52:11,010 --> 00:52:13,050
We flush ourselves in.

539
00:52:17,340 --> 00:52:19,350
Its bloody disgusting.

540
00:52:51,220 --> 00:52:54,660
- You, come along. - What, what?

541
00:52:54,660 --> 00:52:56,780
What did I do?

542
00:53:04,960 --> 00:53:06,900
- Are those...? - Muggles.

543
00:53:07,260 --> 00:53:11,190
In their... rightful place.

544
00:53:13,500 --> 00:53:16,330
Got to tell you, I'm starting to freak out a bit.

545
00:53:19,210 --> 00:53:22,930
How long did you say this batch of polyjuice will last, Hermione?

546
00:53:24,020 --> 00:53:25,680
I didn't.

547
00:53:32,250 --> 00:53:33,940
Cattermole.

548
00:53:35,200 --> 00:53:38,830
Its still raining inside my office. Its two days now.

549
00:53:40,830 --> 00:53:42,540
Have you tried an umbrella?

550
00:53:43,610 --> 00:53:46,450
Do you realize I'm going downstairs don't you, Cattermole?

551
00:53:47,090 --> 00:53:50,420
- Downstairs? - To interrogate your wife.

552
00:53:51,940 --> 00:53:55,640
Now if my wife's blood status were in doubt,

553
00:53:56,210 --> 00:53:57,530
and the Head of Department

554
00:53:57,630 --> 00:54:00,410
of Magical Law Enforcement needed a job doing,

555
00:54:01,070 --> 00:54:04,110
I think I might just make that a priority.

556
00:54:05,210 --> 00:54:07,140
You have one hour.

557
00:54:18,950 --> 00:54:21,740
Oh my god, what am I gonna do?

558
00:54:21,790 --> 00:54:24,350
My wife's all alone downstairs.

559
00:54:24,970 --> 00:54:27,700
Ron, you don't have a wife.

560
00:54:28,720 --> 00:54:30,700
Oh right.

561
00:54:30,720 --> 00:54:31,700
Level Two.

562
00:54:32,290 --> 00:54:34,630
But how do I stop it raining?

563
00:54:34,630 --> 00:54:36,680
Try "Finite Incantatem".

564
00:54:40,870 --> 00:54:42,410
This is you, Ron.

565
00:54:47,160 --> 00:54:49,830
Finite Incantatem, okay.

566
00:54:50,330 --> 00:54:51,770
And if that doesn't work?

567
00:55:07,370 --> 00:55:09,390
I say if we don't locate Umbridge within the hour,

568
00:55:09,470 --> 00:55:11,460
we go find Ron and come back another day.

569
00:55:11,560 --> 00:55:12,610
- Deal? - Yes.

570
00:55:15,750 --> 00:55:18,620
Ah, Mafalda. Trevor sent you, did he?

571
00:55:18,670 --> 00:55:21,450
Good. We'll go straight down.

572
00:55:24,080 --> 00:55:25,900
Albert, weren't you getting out?

573
00:56:00,090 --> 00:56:00,820
Runcorn?

574
00:56:54,540 --> 00:56:55,400
Accio locket!

575
00:57:50,430 --> 00:57:53,580
All right, all right. Let's calm down.

576
00:57:54,620 --> 00:57:57,480
Lets get back to work, please.

577
00:57:58,060 --> 00:57:59,150
Calm down.

578
00:58:05,130 --> 00:58:06,460
Runcorn?

579
00:58:14,480 --> 00:58:16,240
Morning.

580
00:58:18,070 --> 00:58:21,680
- Ron, it's me. - Harry!

581
00:58:21,730 --> 00:58:24,140
Blimey! Forgot what you look like.

582
00:58:24,750 --> 00:58:26,730
Where's Hermione?

583
00:58:26,730 --> 00:58:29,980
She's gone down to the court rooms, with Umbridge.

584
00:58:36,550 --> 00:58:37,710
Bloody cold down here.

585
00:58:38,780 --> 00:58:42,770
I'm half blood. My father, my father was a wizard.

586
00:58:42,820 --> 00:58:45,260
William Waldenten, he worked here for 30 years.

587
00:58:45,310 --> 00:58:48,460
Perhaps you know him. He Always wore a jacket inside out.

588
00:58:48,460 --> 00:58:50,060
There must be a mistake.

589
00:58:50,370 --> 00:58:53,610
Tell the ministry, I must go to work, I'm half blood.

590
00:59:04,720 --> 00:59:07,190
Mary Elizabeth Cattermole,

591
00:59:07,190 --> 00:59:11,940
of 27 Chislehurst Gardens, Great Tolling, Itchum.

592
00:59:11,990 --> 00:59:13,230
- Yes. - It's here.

593
00:59:13,280 --> 00:59:18,090
Mother to Maisie, Ellie and Alfred; Wife to Reginald?

594
00:59:22,450 --> 00:59:23,290
Regi.

595
00:59:34,830 --> 00:59:36,420
Thank you, Albert.

596
00:59:39,380 --> 00:59:41,970
Mary Elizabeth Cattermole.

597
00:59:44,220 --> 00:59:45,220
Yes?

598
00:59:46,400 --> 00:59:47,800
A wand was taken from you upon

599
00:59:47,800 --> 00:59:50,200
your arrival at the Ministry today, Mrs. Cattermole

600
00:59:50,250 --> 00:59:52,650
Is this that wand?

601
00:59:54,760 --> 00:59:56,580
Would you please tell the court,

602
00:59:56,580 --> 00:59:59,200
from which witch or wizard you took this wand?

603
00:59:59,630 --> 01:00:01,520
I didn't take it.

604
01:00:03,110 --> 01:00:08,250
I bought it at Diagon Alley, at Ollivanders, when I was 11.

605
01:00:10,230 --> 01:00:12,070
It chose me.

606
01:00:14,240 --> 01:00:15,320
You're lying.

607
01:00:16,760 --> 01:00:21,300
Wands only choose witches, and you are not a witch.

608
01:00:21,330 --> 01:00:22,420
But I am.

609
01:00:23,800 --> 01:00:26,120
Tell them, Reg, tell them what I am.

610
01:00:29,680 --> 01:00:30,650
Reg, tell them who I am.

611
01:00:40,670 --> 01:00:42,780
What on earth are you doing, Albert?

612
01:00:45,300 --> 01:00:47,100
You're lying, Dolores.

613
01:00:48,690 --> 01:00:51,720
And one mustn't tell lies.

614
01:00:52,940 --> 01:00:54,110
Stupefy!

615
01:01:01,730 --> 01:01:03,360
Oh, it's Harry Potter!

616
01:01:03,360 --> 01:01:06,620
It's him isn't it. This is one to tell the kids.

617
01:01:22,110 --> 01:01:24,000
Expecto patronum!

618
01:01:49,460 --> 01:01:51,800
Mary, go home.

619
01:01:53,020 --> 01:01:53,940
Get the kids.

620
01:01:54,960 --> 01:01:55,730
I'll meet you there.

621
01:01:55,770 --> 01:01:57,410
We have to get out of the country, understand?

622
01:01:58,370 --> 01:01:59,500
Mary, do as I say.

623
01:02:15,060 --> 01:02:16,080
Mary?

624
01:02:17,900 --> 01:02:19,060
Who's that?

625
01:02:20,920 --> 01:02:24,200
Long story, nice meeting you.

626
01:02:24,250 --> 01:02:28,700
- Harry Potter. - It's Harry, Harry Potter.

627
01:03:06,250 --> 01:03:07,700
Expelliarmus!

628
01:04:03,140 --> 01:04:06,070
Harry, Harry, quickly, in my bag.

629
01:04:06,450 --> 01:04:08,270
There's a bottle labeled "Essence of Dittany".

630
01:04:15,770 --> 01:04:16,610
Quickly!

631
01:04:18,290 --> 01:04:19,260
Accio Dittany!

632
01:04:20,440 --> 01:04:23,370
All right, unstopper it.

633
01:04:23,420 --> 01:04:24,670
Hermione, his arm.

634
01:04:24,810 --> 01:04:26,590
I know, just do it!

635
01:04:30,730 --> 01:04:33,320
It's gonna... It's gonna sting a little bit.

636
01:04:33,370 --> 01:04:34,220
What happened?

637
01:04:34,330 --> 01:04:36,090
I thought we were going to go back to Grimmauld Place.

638
01:04:36,140 --> 01:04:39,760
We were. Alright, One more, one more.

639
01:04:39,810 --> 01:04:43,990
We were there we were there but, Yaxley had a hold of me,

640
01:04:44,040 --> 01:04:46,620
I knew once he'd seen where we were we,

641
01:04:46,670 --> 01:04:47,870
we couldn't stay so,

642
01:04:48,360 --> 01:04:49,920
I brought us here, but,

643
01:04:51,280 --> 01:04:53,790
Ron got splinched.

644
01:05:17,950 --> 01:05:19,520
Protego Totalum.

645
01:05:21,700 --> 01:05:24,500
- Salvio Hexia. - What are you doing?

646
01:05:24,950 --> 01:05:26,510
Protective enchantments.

647
01:05:27,410 --> 01:05:28,500
I don't fancy another visit

648
01:05:28,500 --> 01:05:30,540
like the one we had at Shaftesbury Avenue, do you?

649
01:05:31,110 --> 01:05:33,450
You can get going on a tent.

650
01:05:33,500 --> 01:05:34,760
Tent?

651
01:05:35,490 --> 01:05:37,430
- Protego Totalum. - Where am I supposed to find a tent?

652
01:05:38,320 --> 01:05:41,370
Repello Muggletum. Muffliato.

653
01:05:52,470 --> 01:05:53,680
You first.

654
01:06:12,880 --> 01:06:14,140
Incendio.

655
01:06:20,360 --> 01:06:21,470
Expulso!

656
01:06:29,660 --> 01:06:30,760
Diffindo!

657
01:06:33,130 --> 01:06:34,040
Reducto!

658
01:06:55,500 --> 01:06:57,110
What are you doing?

659
01:06:58,970 --> 01:07:01,900
We have to keep it safe, until we find out how to destroy it.

660
01:07:01,910 --> 01:07:02,990
Seems strange, mate.

661
01:07:04,060 --> 01:07:06,130
Dumbledore sent you off to find these Horcruxes,

662
01:07:06,130 --> 01:07:07,580
but doesn't tell you how to destroy them.

663
01:07:08,910 --> 01:07:09,980
Doesn't that bother you?

664
01:07:45,040 --> 01:07:47,450
You know the spell, Harry.

665
01:07:56,240 --> 01:07:59,910
- Tell me, Gregorovitch. - He stole from me.

666
01:08:00,100 --> 01:08:03,160
Who was he, the thief?

667
01:08:06,500 --> 01:08:09,980
The boy. It was he who took it.

668
01:08:10,800 --> 01:08:15,020
I never saw it again, I swear on my life.

669
01:08:16,000 --> 01:08:17,090
I believe you.

670
01:08:23,010 --> 01:08:24,900
Avada Kedavra!

671
01:08:39,480 --> 01:08:40,940
I thought it stopped.

672
01:08:43,110 --> 01:08:44,780
You can't keep letting him in, Harry.

673
01:08:47,600 --> 01:08:51,520
- You-Know-Who has found, Gregorovitch. - The Wand Maker?

674
01:08:51,720 --> 01:08:56,430
He wants something that Gregorovitch used to have.

675
01:08:57,180 --> 01:09:00,650
I don't know what. But he wants it desperately.

676
01:09:01,120 --> 01:09:04,380
I mean, it's as if his life depends on it.

677
01:09:06,300 --> 01:09:08,990
Don't, it comforts him.

678
01:09:09,040 --> 01:09:10,420
It sets my teeth on edge.

679
01:09:10,480 --> 01:09:12,170
What's he expecting to hear, good news?

680
01:09:15,290 --> 01:09:17,820
I think he just hopes that he doesn't hear bad news.

681
01:09:20,730 --> 01:09:21,940
How long before he can travel?

682
01:09:25,050 --> 01:09:28,000
- I.. I'm doing everything I can. - You're not doing enough.

683
01:09:31,310 --> 01:09:32,230
Take it off!

684
01:09:34,010 --> 01:09:35,590
I said, Take it off, now!

685
01:09:47,590 --> 01:09:49,970
- Better? - Right.

686
01:09:53,810 --> 01:09:55,630
We'll take it in turns, okay?

687
01:10:30,510 --> 01:10:33,520
Severus Snape voted in as headmaster of Hogwarts.

688
01:11:38,630 --> 01:11:39,650
What's that?

689
01:11:49,200 --> 01:11:51,190
What's that, smell?

690
01:12:14,410 --> 01:12:16,340
Whatcha doing? It's heavy.

691
01:12:16,690 --> 01:12:20,730
Oh I'm sorry. Do you want me to carry it?

692
01:12:29,160 --> 01:12:30,000
Snatchers.

693
01:12:31,850 --> 01:12:33,450
Good to know your enchantments work.

694
01:12:39,480 --> 01:12:42,550
He could smell it, my perfume.

695
01:12:45,660 --> 01:12:46,430
I told you,

696
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:49,730
Ron isn't strong enough to apparate.

697
01:12:49,920 --> 01:12:52,880
Well then, we'll go on foot.

698
01:12:54,640 --> 01:12:57,080
Only next time, as much as you like your perfume,

699
01:12:57,080 --> 01:12:58,790
just don't wear any.

700
01:13:04,240 --> 01:13:07,100
And now for the names of missing witches and wizards.

701
01:13:09,070 --> 01:13:10,270
These are confirmed,

702
01:13:11,690 --> 01:13:14,230
thankfully the list is short today.

703
01:13:16,280 --> 01:13:18,550
Jason and Alison Denbright.

704
01:13:19,350 --> 01:13:20,090
Oh, thank you.

705
01:13:20,090 --> 01:13:23,130
Bella, Jake, Charlie, and Madge Farley.

706
01:13:24,130 --> 01:13:25,170
Joe Laurie.

707
01:13:26,370 --> 01:13:28,380
Eleanor Sarah Gibbs.

708
01:13:30,270 --> 01:13:32,620
Harry and Bronwyn Trigg.

709
01:13:35,330 --> 01:13:37,330
Rob and Ellie Dowson.

710
01:13:39,300 --> 01:13:41,020
Georgia Clark-Day.

711
01:13:42,610 --> 01:13:44,040
Joshua Flexson.

712
01:13:45,590 --> 01:13:46,980
George Coutas.

713
01:13:48,000 --> 01:13:50,350
Gabriella and Emily Mather.

714
01:13:51,890 --> 01:13:54,290
Jacob and Mimi Erland.

715
01:13:54,900 --> 01:13:58,170
William and Brian Gallagher.

716
01:13:58,210 --> 01:13:59,750
He doesn't know what he's doing, does he?

717
01:14:03,130 --> 01:14:04,410
None of us do.

718
01:14:11,140 --> 01:14:13,310
Katie and James Killick.

719
01:14:14,180 --> 01:14:16,210
Elsie Valentine Schroeder.

720
01:14:17,670 --> 01:14:18,620
Jennifer Winston.

721
01:14:19,780 --> 01:14:22,130
Tamsin and Iola Hillicker.

722
01:14:44,150 --> 01:14:47,450
- Oh My God! - What?

723
01:14:48,670 --> 01:14:49,740
I'll tell you in a minute.

724
01:14:51,250 --> 01:14:52,760
Maybe you can tell me now.

725
01:14:54,240 --> 01:14:57,510
Sword of Gryffindor. It's goblin made.

726
01:14:57,510 --> 01:14:58,900
Brilliant.

727
01:14:59,590 --> 01:15:01,330
No, you don't understand.

728
01:15:02,210 --> 01:15:04,990
Dirt and rust have no effect on the blade.

729
01:15:05,750 --> 01:15:08,240
It only takes in that which makes it stronger.

730
01:15:09,500 --> 01:15:11,130
O... kay.

731
01:15:11,140 --> 01:15:13,950
Harry, we've already destroyed one horcrux, right?

732
01:15:14,670 --> 01:15:16,320
Tom Riddle's diary in the Chamber of Secrets.

733
01:15:16,320 --> 01:15:18,960
With a basilisk fang.

734
01:15:18,960 --> 01:15:20,070
If you tell me you've got one of those

735
01:15:20,070 --> 01:15:21,850
in that bloody beaded bag of yours...

736
01:15:21,850 --> 01:15:22,760
Don't you see?

737
01:15:24,190 --> 01:15:25,010
In The Chamber of Secrets,

738
01:15:25,040 --> 01:15:27,920
you stabbed the Basilisk with the sword of Gryffindor.

739
01:15:27,920 --> 01:15:30,990
Its blade is impregnated with basilisk venom.

740
01:15:31,510 --> 01:15:33,740
It only takes in that which makes it stronger.

741
01:15:33,740 --> 01:15:37,100
- Exactly, which is why... - It can destroy Horcruxes.

742
01:15:37,430 --> 01:15:39,510
That's why Dumbledore left it to you in his will.

743
01:15:39,510 --> 01:15:43,610
You're brilliant, Hermione. Truly.

744
01:15:44,020 --> 01:15:45,610
Actually, I'm highly logical

745
01:15:45,610 --> 01:15:48,340
which allows me to slip past extraneous details.

746
01:15:48,340 --> 01:15:50,410
And perceive clearly that which others overlook.

747
01:15:50,410 --> 01:15:52,850
Yeah, there is only one problem with this.

748
01:15:59,140 --> 01:16:00,760
The sword was stolen.

749
01:16:02,630 --> 01:16:05,120
Yeah, I'm still here.

750
01:16:05,920 --> 01:16:06,740
But you two carry on.

751
01:16:07,300 --> 01:16:09,110
Don't let me spoil the fun.

752
01:16:11,260 --> 01:16:14,260
- What's wrong? - Wrong? Nothing's wrong.

753
01:16:15,160 --> 01:16:16,690
According to you, anyway.

754
01:16:17,090 --> 01:16:19,040
If you got something to say, don't be shy.

755
01:16:20,120 --> 01:16:20,820
Spit it out.

756
01:16:21,320 --> 01:16:23,250
Alright, I'll spit it out.

757
01:16:23,670 --> 01:16:25,090
But don't expect me to be grateful

758
01:16:25,090 --> 01:16:27,440
just because now it's another damn thing we got to find.

759
01:16:27,440 --> 01:16:29,200
I thought you knew what you signed up for.

760
01:16:29,200 --> 01:16:31,430
Yeah, I thought it too.

761
01:16:32,010 --> 01:16:34,840
I'm sorry. But I don't quite understand.

762
01:16:35,480 --> 01:16:38,290
What part of this isn't living up to your expectations?

763
01:16:39,110 --> 01:16:41,320
Did you think we were going to be staying in a five star hotel?

764
01:16:41,320 --> 01:16:42,890
Finding a Horcrux every other day.

765
01:16:43,120 --> 01:16:45,200
You thought you'd be back with your mum by Christmas?

766
01:16:45,200 --> 01:16:46,670
I just thought, after all this time

767
01:16:46,670 --> 01:16:48,980
we would actually have achieved something.

768
01:16:48,980 --> 01:16:50,280
I thought you knew what you were doing.

769
01:16:50,290 --> 01:16:52,550
I thought Dumbledore would have told you something worthwhile.

770
01:16:52,550 --> 01:16:53,300
I thought you had a plan.

771
01:16:53,300 --> 01:16:55,920
I told you everything Dumbledore told me.

772
01:16:55,920 --> 01:16:58,550
And in case you haven't notice we have found a Horcrux already.

773
01:16:58,550 --> 01:17:00,200
and we're as close to getting rid of it

774
01:17:00,320 --> 01:17:01,930
as we are to finding the rest of them, aren't we?

775
01:17:03,430 --> 01:17:07,310
Ron, Please, take off the Horcrux.

776
01:17:07,310 --> 01:17:08,200
You wouldn't be saying any of this

777
01:17:08,210 --> 01:17:09,800
if you hadn't been wearing it all day.

778
01:17:09,800 --> 01:17:12,300
You don't know, why I listen to the radio every night, do you?

779
01:17:12,510 --> 01:17:15,500
To make sure I don't hear Ginny's name,

780
01:17:15,500 --> 01:17:17,570
or Fred, or George or Moms.

781
01:17:17,570 --> 01:17:19,290
You think I'm not listening too?

782
01:17:19,410 --> 01:17:21,030
You think I don't know how it feels?

783
01:17:21,030 --> 01:17:22,440
No you don't know how it feels!

784
01:17:22,440 --> 01:17:25,610
Your parents are dead! You have no family!

785
01:17:26,200 --> 01:17:27,280
Stop! Stop!

786
01:17:27,420 --> 01:17:30,630
- Let me go! - Go then!

787
01:17:38,070 --> 01:17:39,110
Ron!

788
01:17:42,920 --> 01:17:44,160
And you?

789
01:17:46,380 --> 01:17:48,400
Are you coming or are you staying?

790
01:17:55,970 --> 01:18:01,410
Fine, I get it. I saw you two the other night.

791
01:18:02,160 --> 01:18:04,580
Ron there's... there's nothing.

792
01:18:06,660 --> 01:18:07,680
Ron!

793
01:18:11,370 --> 01:18:12,880
Ron, where are you going?

794
01:18:15,090 --> 01:18:16,440
Come back!

795
01:18:18,260 --> 01:18:19,400
Ron!

796
01:18:24,420 --> 01:18:25,560
Ron!

797
01:19:39,670 --> 01:19:41,500
Salvia Hexia.

798
01:22:49,370 --> 01:22:50,870
I open at the close.

799
01:22:53,040 --> 01:22:55,700
Hermione. Hermione.

800
01:22:55,700 --> 01:22:58,820
You were right. Snitches have flesh memories.

801
01:22:58,820 --> 01:23:00,900
But I didn't catch the first snitch with my hand.

802
01:23:00,900 --> 01:23:02,740
I almost swallowed it.

803
01:23:08,880 --> 01:23:11,710
- "I open at the close. " - Yeah, what do you think that means?

804
01:23:11,720 --> 01:23:13,000
I don't know.

805
01:23:15,560 --> 01:23:17,190
I found something as well.

806
01:23:24,330 --> 01:23:27,400
At first I thought it was an eye, but now I don't think it is.

807
01:23:27,910 --> 01:23:32,030
It isn't a rune, and it isn't anywhere in Spellman's syllabary.

808
01:23:32,560 --> 01:23:34,120
Somebody inked it in.

809
01:23:34,120 --> 01:23:36,020
It isn't part of the book, somebody drew it.

810
01:23:36,020 --> 01:23:38,950
Luna's dad was wearing it at Bill and Fleur's wedding.

811
01:23:42,180 --> 01:23:44,690
Why would someone draw it in a children's book?

812
01:23:48,130 --> 01:23:49,990
Hermione, I've been thinking.

813
01:23:51,090 --> 01:23:53,130
I want to go to Godric's Hollow.

814
01:23:53,380 --> 01:23:56,430
It's where I was born, It's where my parents died.

815
01:23:56,710 --> 01:23:57,830
That's exactly where he'll expect you to go

816
01:23:57,830 --> 01:24:00,130
because it means something to you.

817
01:24:00,130 --> 01:24:03,040
But it means something to him too, Hermione.

818
01:24:03,070 --> 01:24:05,180
You-Know-Who almost died there.

819
01:24:05,180 --> 01:24:07,130
Isn't that exactly the type of place

820
01:24:07,130 --> 01:24:09,020
he'd be likely to hide a Horcrux?

821
01:24:10,480 --> 01:24:12,720
I... it's dangerous, Harry.

822
01:24:15,090 --> 01:24:16,330
But even I have to admit

823
01:24:16,330 --> 01:24:18,820
recently I've been thinking we have to go there.

824
01:24:19,310 --> 01:24:21,700
I think it's possible something else is hidden there.

825
01:24:21,700 --> 01:24:22,840
What?

826
01:24:23,990 --> 01:24:25,250
The Sword.

827
01:24:26,340 --> 01:24:28,320
If Dumbledore wanted you to find it,

828
01:24:28,320 --> 01:24:30,300
and didn't want it to falling in to the Ministry hands,

829
01:24:30,300 --> 01:24:31,670
where better to hide it than

830
01:24:31,670 --> 01:24:33,780
the birthplace of the founder of Gryffindor.

831
01:24:35,840 --> 01:24:37,170
Hermione.

832
01:24:42,860 --> 01:24:45,000
Don't ever let me give you a haircut again.

833
01:25:07,040 --> 01:25:09,190
I still think that we should use the Polyjuice Potion.

834
01:25:09,760 --> 01:25:13,540
No, this is where I was born.

835
01:25:14,540 --> 01:25:16,210
I'm not returning as someone else.

836
01:25:32,870 --> 01:25:34,850
Harry, I think it's Christmas eve.

837
01:25:36,950 --> 01:25:38,190
Listen.

838
01:25:44,120 --> 01:25:46,500
Do you think they may be in there, Hermione?

839
01:25:46,500 --> 01:25:48,640
My Mom and Dad.

840
01:25:55,210 --> 01:25:57,200
Yeah, I think they would.

841
01:26:34,070 --> 01:26:36,950
Ignotus Peverell.

842
01:26:38,770 --> 01:26:40,490
Hey, Harry?

843
01:27:18,780 --> 01:27:19,420
Merry Christmas, Hermione.

844
01:27:22,160 --> 01:27:23,800
Merry Christmas, Harry.

845
01:27:44,340 --> 01:27:46,540
Harry, there is someone watching us.

846
01:27:47,160 --> 01:27:48,640
By the church.

847
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:01,610
I think I know who that is.

848
01:28:04,300 --> 01:28:08,040
- I don't like this, Harry. - Hermione, she knew Dumbledore.

849
01:28:08,090 --> 01:28:09,810
She might have the sword.

850
01:28:29,730 --> 01:28:31,600
This is where they died, Hermione.

851
01:28:38,820 --> 01:28:40,560
This is where he murdered them.

852
01:28:53,800 --> 01:28:55,450
You're Bathilda, aren't you?

853
01:29:01,500 --> 01:29:03,060
Here, let me do that.

854
01:29:27,620 --> 01:29:30,830
Miss Bagshot, who is this man?

855
01:29:43,000 --> 01:29:44,150
Harry.

856
01:31:31,220 --> 01:31:32,170
Harry!

857
01:33:06,700 --> 01:33:08,120
Are you feeling better?

858
01:33:11,820 --> 01:33:14,290
You've outdone yourself this time, Hermione.

859
01:33:14,640 --> 01:33:16,090
Forest of Dean.

860
01:33:17,780 --> 01:33:21,480
I came here once with Mum and Dad. Years ago.

861
01:33:22,770 --> 01:33:24,250
It's just how I remember it.

862
01:33:25,110 --> 01:33:28,540
The trees, the river, everything.

863
01:33:29,410 --> 01:33:31,460
Like nothings changed.

864
01:33:33,610 --> 01:33:35,870
Not true of course, everything's changed.

865
01:33:37,180 --> 01:33:38,980
If I brought my parents back here now,

866
01:33:38,980 --> 01:33:40,630
they probably wouldn't recognize any of it.

867
01:33:43,500 --> 01:33:44,820
Not the trees.

868
01:33:45,690 --> 01:33:46,870
Not the river.

869
01:33:49,260 --> 01:33:50,670
Not even me.

870
01:33:56,600 --> 01:33:58,740
Maybe we should just stay here, Harry.

871
01:34:01,420 --> 01:34:02,880
Grow old.

872
01:34:09,560 --> 01:34:12,140
You wanted to know who was the boy in the photograph was.

873
01:34:13,560 --> 01:34:14,840
I know.

874
01:34:15,800 --> 01:34:18,240
Gellert Grindelwald.

875
01:34:25,300 --> 01:34:28,050
He's the thief I saw in Gregorovitch's wand shop.

876
01:34:28,340 --> 01:34:31,730
Speaking of which, where is my wand?

877
01:34:33,330 --> 01:34:35,180
Where's my wand, Hermione?

878
01:34:44,470 --> 01:34:46,020
As we were leaving Godrics Hollow

879
01:34:46,020 --> 01:34:48,350
I cast a curse and it rebounded.

880
01:34:51,520 --> 01:34:53,100
I'm sorry.

881
01:34:53,440 --> 01:34:55,080
I tried to mend it, but wands are different.

882
01:34:55,090 --> 01:34:56,330
It's done.

883
01:34:58,020 --> 01:34:59,580
Leave me yours.

884
01:35:00,020 --> 01:35:01,750
Go inside and get warm.

885
01:35:02,440 --> 01:35:04,200
I'll take the locket as well.

886
01:36:44,530 --> 01:36:45,640
Lumos.

887
01:37:27,240 --> 01:37:28,680
Accio sword!

888
01:37:34,290 --> 01:37:35,590
Diffindo.

889
01:39:16,590 --> 01:39:17,690
Hermione?

890
01:39:17,990 --> 01:39:19,260
Are you mental?

891
01:39:21,050 --> 01:39:22,250
It was you.

892
01:39:22,950 --> 01:39:25,910
Well yeah, bit obvious, I think.

893
01:39:26,260 --> 01:39:28,250
And you cast the doe as well did you?

894
01:39:29,040 --> 01:39:30,390
No, I thought that was you.

895
01:39:30,390 --> 01:39:32,350
No, my Patronus was a stag.

896
01:39:32,900 --> 01:39:35,870
Right, now that was...

897
01:39:38,440 --> 01:39:41,210
Okay, Ron. Do it.

898
01:39:42,510 --> 01:39:44,340
I can't handle it.

899
01:39:44,340 --> 01:39:47,610
That thing affect me more than it effects you and Hermione.

900
01:39:47,610 --> 01:39:49,670
- All the more reason. - No, I can't.

901
01:39:49,670 --> 01:39:51,170
Then why are you here?

902
01:39:52,070 --> 01:39:53,670
Why did you come back?

903
01:40:01,840 --> 01:40:05,080
Now I'll have to speak to it in order for it to open.

904
01:40:05,080 --> 01:40:06,250
When it does, don't hesitate.

905
01:40:06,670 --> 01:40:08,860
I don't know what's in there, but it will put up a fight.

906
01:40:08,860 --> 01:40:11,320
The bit of Riddle that was in that diary tried to kill me.

907
01:40:16,880 --> 01:40:17,950
One.

908
01:40:19,080 --> 01:40:20,150
Two.

909
01:40:20,940 --> 01:40:22,060
Three.

910
01:40:33,240 --> 01:40:37,500
I have seen your heart and it is mine.

911
01:40:40,720 --> 01:40:44,120
I have seen your dreams, Ronald Weasley.

912
01:40:44,440 --> 01:40:46,860
And I see your fears.

913
01:40:48,860 --> 01:40:52,550
Least loved by your mother, who craved a daughter.

914
01:40:53,640 --> 01:40:57,940
Least loved by the girl, who prefers your friend.

915
01:40:59,370 --> 01:41:01,040
Ron, kill it!

916
01:41:07,950 --> 01:41:09,880
We were better without you.

917
01:41:11,250 --> 01:41:13,280
Happy without you.

918
01:41:13,280 --> 01:41:17,880
Who would look at you? Who has, Harry Potter.

919
01:41:21,710 --> 01:41:23,140
What are you, compared to the chosen one?

920
01:41:23,200 --> 01:41:24,460
Ron, it's lying!

921
01:41:24,690 --> 01:41:27,650
Your mother confessed, she would prefer me as a son.

922
01:41:27,690 --> 01:41:29,720
What woman would take you?

923
01:41:30,870 --> 01:41:35,230
You are nothing... nothing.

924
01:41:36,490 --> 01:41:39,600
Nothing compared to him.

925
01:42:30,740 --> 01:42:34,730
Just think.

926
01:42:34,730 --> 01:42:35,730
There are only three to go.

927
01:42:38,230 --> 01:42:39,350
Hermione?

928
01:42:42,270 --> 01:42:43,190
Hermione?

929
01:42:48,520 --> 01:42:50,060
Is everything alright?

930
01:42:51,520 --> 01:42:55,140
It's fine. Actually, yeah, it's more than fine.

931
01:43:00,500 --> 01:43:01,420
Hey.

932
01:43:06,300 --> 01:43:07,600
You...

933
01:43:07,840 --> 01:43:11,670
...A complete ass, Ronald Weasley!

934
01:43:12,420 --> 01:43:16,100
You show up here after weeks and you say 'hey'?

935
01:43:18,660 --> 01:43:19,630
Where's my wand, Harry?

936
01:43:20,080 --> 01:43:21,290
- Where's my wand? - I don't know.

937
01:43:21,630 --> 01:43:23,330
Harry Potter. You give me my wand!

938
01:43:23,770 --> 01:43:26,710
- How come he's got your wand? - Never mind why's he got my wand.

939
01:43:29,950 --> 01:43:31,150
What is that?

940
01:43:34,190 --> 01:43:35,470
You destroyed it.

941
01:43:38,480 --> 01:43:39,560
And how is it that you just

942
01:43:39,560 --> 01:43:41,740
happen to have the sword of Gryffindor?

943
01:43:42,620 --> 01:43:43,930
It's a long story.

944
01:43:47,890 --> 01:43:49,820
Don't think this changes anything.

945
01:43:50,340 --> 01:43:53,280
Of course not. I only just destroyed a bloody Horcrux,

946
01:43:53,290 --> 01:43:55,120
why will that change anything.

947
01:43:55,670 --> 01:43:59,040
Look, I wanted to come back as soon as I left.

948
01:44:00,000 --> 01:44:01,270
I just didn't know how to find you.

949
01:44:01,270 --> 01:44:02,810
Yeah, how did you find us?

950
01:44:03,670 --> 01:44:06,460
With this. Doesn't just turn off lights.

951
01:44:06,740 --> 01:44:08,430
I don't know how it works,

952
01:44:08,430 --> 01:44:11,640
but Christmas morning I sleeping in this little pub.

953
01:44:11,790 --> 01:44:13,530
Keeping away from some snatchers.

954
01:44:14,450 --> 01:44:17,050
- When I heard it. - It?

955
01:44:19,250 --> 01:44:20,500
A voice.

956
01:44:22,730 --> 01:44:24,140
Your voice, Hermione.

957
01:44:25,010 --> 01:44:26,370
Comin' out of it.

958
01:44:26,780 --> 01:44:29,020
And what exactly did I say if I may ask?

959
01:44:29,160 --> 01:44:30,170
My name.

960
01:44:31,150 --> 01:44:32,440
Just my name.

961
01:44:33,920 --> 01:44:35,610
Like a whisper.

962
01:44:37,960 --> 01:44:40,780
So I took it, clicked it...

963
01:44:41,550 --> 01:44:43,510
and this tiny ball of light appeared.

964
01:44:44,700 --> 01:44:47,860
And I knew, sure enough.

965
01:44:48,630 --> 01:44:50,930
It floated towards me, the ball of light.

966
01:44:53,050 --> 01:44:57,470
Went right to my chest, straight through me. Right here.

967
01:44:58,560 --> 01:44:59,780
I knew it was gonna take me where I needed to go,

968
01:44:59,780 --> 01:45:01,970
so I disapparated.

969
01:45:02,410 --> 01:45:04,040
I came to this hillside.

970
01:45:05,030 --> 01:45:07,760
It was dark, I had no idea where I was.

971
01:45:08,230 --> 01:45:10,630
I just hoped that one of you would show yourself.

972
01:45:12,300 --> 01:45:13,440
You did.

973
01:45:30,840 --> 01:45:33,330
I've always liked these flames Hermione makes.

974
01:45:37,860 --> 01:45:39,940
How long do you reckon she'll stay mad at me?

975
01:45:41,920 --> 01:45:45,340
Just keep talking about that little ball of light touching your heart.

976
01:45:45,720 --> 01:45:49,230
- And she'll come around. - It's true. Every word.

977
01:45:51,570 --> 01:45:53,300
This is gonna sound crazy.

978
01:45:54,640 --> 01:45:56,760
But I think, thats why Dumbledore left it to me.

979
01:45:57,020 --> 01:45:57,860
The Deluminator.

980
01:45:59,520 --> 01:46:01,930
I think he knew that somehow I'd need to find my way back.

981
01:46:01,930 --> 01:46:03,600
That she'd lead me.

982
01:46:07,310 --> 01:46:10,150
You know, I just realized. You need a wand, don't you?

983
01:46:10,160 --> 01:46:12,030
- Yeah. - I got one here.

984
01:46:12,990 --> 01:46:16,890
It's a Blackthorn, 10 inches, nothing special.

985
01:46:16,890 --> 01:46:18,710
I reckon it'll do.

986
01:46:19,730 --> 01:46:21,790
Took it off a snatcher a couple of weeks ago.

987
01:46:22,820 --> 01:46:24,320
Don't tell Hermione this.

988
01:46:24,420 --> 01:46:26,090
They're a bit dim, snatchers.

989
01:46:26,890 --> 01:46:31,330
This one is definitely partial to smelling.

990
01:46:31,480 --> 01:46:32,570
- Engorgio. - Put it out.

991
01:46:32,580 --> 01:46:34,330
What's going on in there?

992
01:46:34,330 --> 01:46:35,030
- Nothing! - Nothing!

993
01:46:37,470 --> 01:46:38,740
We need to talk.

994
01:46:40,230 --> 01:46:41,590
Yeah, alright.

995
01:46:47,960 --> 01:46:50,210
I want to go see Xenophilius Lovegood.

996
01:46:50,650 --> 01:46:51,660
Sorry?

997
01:46:53,300 --> 01:46:57,480
See this? It's a letter Dumbledore wrote to Grindelwald.

998
01:46:57,650 --> 01:46:58,710
Look at the signature.

999
01:47:00,390 --> 01:47:01,500
It's the mark again.

1000
01:47:03,540 --> 01:47:05,010
It keeps cropping up.

1001
01:47:05,980 --> 01:47:09,240
In Beedle the Bard, in the graveyard in Godric's Hollow.

1002
01:47:10,780 --> 01:47:12,290
It was there too.

1003
01:47:13,070 --> 01:47:15,750
- Where? - Outside Gregorvitch's wand shop.

1004
01:47:17,200 --> 01:47:19,190
- What does it mean? - Look.

1005
01:47:19,670 --> 01:47:22,430
You've got no idea where the next Horcrux is, and neither do I.

1006
01:47:24,690 --> 01:47:27,150
But this, this means something.

1007
01:47:28,180 --> 01:47:29,080
I'm sure of it.

1008
01:47:29,080 --> 01:47:31,120
Yeah. Hermione's right.

1009
01:47:32,520 --> 01:47:34,020
We ought to see Lovegood.

1010
01:47:35,430 --> 01:47:36,070
Let's vote on it.

1011
01:47:37,070 --> 01:47:38,010
Those in favor.

1012
01:48:02,780 --> 01:48:04,560
You're not still mad at him, are you?

1013
01:48:05,680 --> 01:48:07,320
I'm always mad at him.

1014
01:48:10,450 --> 01:48:13,500
Luna, we're here.

1015
01:48:14,520 --> 01:48:16,540
Keep off the Dirigible Plums.

1016
01:48:21,740 --> 01:48:23,540
Keep off the Dirigible Plums.

1017
01:48:33,670 --> 01:48:36,140
What is it? Who are you?

1018
01:48:36,650 --> 01:48:37,570
What do you want?

1019
01:48:37,830 --> 01:48:39,450
Hello, Mr. Lovegood.

1020
01:48:39,760 --> 01:48:42,340
I'm Harry Potter, we met a few months ago.

1021
01:48:46,520 --> 01:48:47,730
Can we come in?

1022
01:48:52,060 --> 01:48:54,070
- Where is Luna? - Luna?

1023
01:48:55,840 --> 01:48:57,270
She'll be along.

1024
01:49:08,400 --> 01:49:13,600
So, how can I help you, Mr. Potter?

1025
01:49:14,470 --> 01:49:16,630
Well, actually,

1026
01:49:18,510 --> 01:49:20,890
it was about something you were wearing around your neck at the wedding.

1027
01:49:20,890 --> 01:49:22,170
It was a symbol.

1028
01:49:24,650 --> 01:49:27,530
- You mean this? - Yes.

1029
01:49:28,730 --> 01:49:30,330
That's it exactly.

1030
01:49:31,220 --> 01:49:35,270
What we wondered is... what is it?

1031
01:49:35,630 --> 01:49:36,700
What is it?

1032
01:49:37,320 --> 01:49:40,390
Well, it's the sign of the Deathly Hallows, of course.

1033
01:49:40,430 --> 01:49:41,910
- The What? - The What?

1034
01:49:42,120 --> 01:49:43,050
The Deathly Hallows.

1035
01:49:43,050 --> 01:49:47,240
I assume you are all familiar with the tale of the three brothers.

1036
01:49:47,240 --> 01:49:48,080
- Yes... - Yes.

1037
01:49:48,080 --> 01:49:48,930
No.

1038
01:49:54,190 --> 01:49:55,660
I have it in here.

1039
01:50:06,820 --> 01:50:08,130
There were once three brothers,

1040
01:50:08,130 --> 01:50:12,070
who were traveling along a lonely winding road...

1041
01:50:12,470 --> 01:50:14,590
- At twilight. - Midnight.

1042
01:50:15,430 --> 01:50:16,960
Mom always said midnight.

1043
01:50:21,590 --> 01:50:23,310
Twilight's fine, better actually.

1044
01:50:27,320 --> 01:50:30,520
- Do you want to read it? - Uh, no.

1045
01:50:33,540 --> 01:50:37,050
There were once three brothers, who were traveling along...

1046
01:50:37,320 --> 01:50:38,610
a lonely winding road...

1047
01:50:39,050 --> 01:50:39,840
At twilight.

1048
01:50:42,650 --> 01:50:45,140
In time the brothers reached

1049
01:50:45,140 --> 01:50:47,260
a river too treacherous to pass.

1050
01:50:48,490 --> 01:50:52,650
But they were learned in the magical arts,

1051
01:50:53,210 --> 01:50:54,780
the three brothers simply waved their wands, and made a bridge.

1052
01:50:57,000 --> 01:50:59,170
Before they could cross however,

1053
01:50:59,170 --> 01:51:02,700
they found their path blocked by a hooded figure.

1054
01:51:03,530 --> 01:51:05,000
It was Death.

1055
01:51:05,310 --> 01:51:06,850
And he felt cheated.

1056
01:51:07,780 --> 01:51:08,330
Cheated,

1057
01:51:08,330 --> 01:51:10,710
because travelers would always drown in the river.

1058
01:51:10,780 --> 01:51:12,260
But Death was cunning.

1059
01:51:13,260 --> 01:51:16,880
He pretended to congratulate the three brothers on their magic.

1060
01:51:17,090 --> 01:51:19,740
And said, that each had earned a prize for having

1061
01:51:19,740 --> 01:51:21,310
been clever enough to evade him.

1062
01:51:22,600 --> 01:51:27,320
The oldest asked for a wand, more powerful than any in existence.

1063
01:51:27,420 --> 01:51:28,720
So death fashioned him a

1064
01:51:28,720 --> 01:51:31,070
wand from an elder tree that stood nearby.

1065
01:51:33,130 --> 01:51:37,610
The second brother decided he wanted to humiliate death even further,

1066
01:51:37,930 --> 01:51:41,370
and asked for the power to recall loved ones from the grave.

1067
01:51:42,770 --> 01:51:46,300
So Death plucked a stone from the river and offered it to him.

1068
01:51:47,710 --> 01:51:50,950
Finally, Death turned to the third brother.

1069
01:51:52,830 --> 01:51:54,590
A humble man,

1070
01:51:54,600 --> 01:51:58,630
he asked for something that would allow him to go forth from that place,

1071
01:51:58,730 --> 01:52:01,150
without being followed by death.

1072
01:52:03,030 --> 01:52:08,290
And so it was that death reluctantly handed over his own cloak of invisibility.

1073
01:52:12,670 --> 01:52:15,150
The first brother traveled to a distant village.

1074
01:52:15,400 --> 01:52:17,450
While with the elder wand in hand,

1075
01:52:17,450 --> 01:52:20,800
he killed a wizard with whom he had once quarrels.

1076
01:52:23,570 --> 01:52:26,210
Drunk with the power that the

1077
01:52:26,210 --> 01:52:27,210
elder wand had given him.

1078
01:52:27,590 --> 01:52:29,770
He bragged of his invincibility.

1079
01:52:33,380 --> 01:52:34,740
But that night...

1080
01:52:35,460 --> 01:52:37,070
Another wizard stole the wand

1081
01:52:37,070 --> 01:52:39,640
and slit the brother's throat for good measure.

1082
01:52:40,440 --> 01:52:42,990
And so death took the first brother for his own.

1083
01:52:44,750 --> 01:52:46,460
The second brother journeyed to his home.

1084
01:52:46,460 --> 01:52:49,370
Where he took the stone and turned it twice in hand.

1085
01:52:49,820 --> 01:52:50,980
To his delight

1086
01:52:51,010 --> 01:52:54,120
the girl he'd once hoped to marry before her untimely death,

1087
01:52:54,730 --> 01:52:56,130
appeared before him.

1088
01:52:57,330 --> 01:53:00,110
Yet soon she turned sad and cold

1089
01:53:00,140 --> 01:53:02,310
for she did not belong in the mortal world.

1090
01:53:02,860 --> 01:53:04,740
Driven mad with hopeless longing,

1091
01:53:04,740 --> 01:53:07,580
the second brother killed himself so as to join her.

1092
01:53:09,320 --> 01:53:11,810
And so death took the second brother.

1093
01:53:12,450 --> 01:53:15,230
As for the third brother, Death searched for many years

1094
01:53:15,240 --> 01:53:18,020
but was never able to find him.

1095
01:53:18,790 --> 01:53:20,670
Only when he had attained a great age did the youngest brother,

1096
01:53:20,670 --> 01:53:25,140
shed the cloak of invisibility and give it to his son.

1097
01:53:27,340 --> 01:53:29,620
He then greeted death as a old friend

1098
01:53:30,160 --> 01:53:34,660
and went with him gladly departing this life as equals.

1099
01:53:36,650 --> 01:53:40,640
So there you are. Those are the Deathly Hallows.

1100
01:53:42,750 --> 01:53:45,080
I'm sorry sir, I still don't quite understand.

1101
01:54:04,360 --> 01:54:05,920
The Elder wand.

1102
01:54:07,030 --> 01:54:09,640
The most powerful wand ever made.

1103
01:54:20,750 --> 01:54:22,830
The resurrection stone.

1104
01:54:33,410 --> 01:54:36,790
The cloak of invisibility.

1105
01:54:39,870 --> 01:54:42,170
Together, they make the Deathly Hallows.

1106
01:54:43,210 --> 01:54:48,290
Together, they make one master of death.

1107
01:54:53,750 --> 01:54:57,070
That mark was on the grave in Godrics Hollow.

1108
01:54:59,610 --> 01:55:00,790
Um, Mr. Lovegood,

1109
01:55:00,790 --> 01:55:01,780
does the Peverell family

1110
01:55:01,780 --> 01:55:03,640
have anything to do with the Deathly Hallows?

1111
01:55:06,870 --> 01:55:10,940
Ignotus, excuse me. And his brothers Cadmus and Antioch,

1112
01:55:10,960 --> 01:55:13,830
thought to be the original owners of the Hallows,

1113
01:55:14,140 --> 01:55:15,690
and therefore the inspiration for the story.

1114
01:55:18,380 --> 01:55:20,050
But your tea has gone cold.

1115
01:55:21,950 --> 01:55:23,730
I'll be right back.

1116
01:55:28,200 --> 01:55:28,980
Let's get out of here.

1117
01:55:28,990 --> 01:55:30,940
I don't want to drink anymore of that stuff.

1118
01:55:30,940 --> 01:55:32,300
Hot or cold.

1119
01:55:38,630 --> 01:55:43,270
- Thank you, Sir. - You forgot the water.

1120
01:55:43,610 --> 01:55:46,140
- Water? - For the tea.

1121
01:55:51,190 --> 01:55:52,500
How silly of me.

1122
01:55:54,900 --> 01:55:57,060
It's really nice sir, but we really should be going any way.

1123
01:55:57,210 --> 01:55:58,370
No, you do not!

1124
01:56:03,400 --> 01:56:04,580
Sir?

1125
01:56:12,630 --> 01:56:14,240
You're my only hope.

1126
01:56:19,110 --> 01:56:23,080
They were angry, you see, from what I've been writing.

1127
01:56:26,270 --> 01:56:27,840
So they took her.

1128
01:56:29,870 --> 01:56:31,830
They took my children.

1129
01:56:33,800 --> 01:56:35,180
My children.

1130
01:56:48,470 --> 01:56:51,090
Oh, it's really you, then it'll work.

1131
01:56:53,710 --> 01:56:56,810
Who took her, sir?

1132
01:57:00,690 --> 01:57:02,360
Voldemort.

1133
01:57:14,380 --> 01:57:15,650
I got him!

1134
01:57:32,580 --> 01:57:34,230
Treacherous little bleeder!

1135
01:57:34,230 --> 01:57:36,050
Is there no one we can trust?

1136
01:57:36,510 --> 01:57:38,780
They kidnapped her because he supported me.

1137
01:57:38,900 --> 01:57:40,350
He was just desperate.

1138
01:57:41,820 --> 01:57:43,260
I'll do the enchantments.

1139
01:57:55,670 --> 01:57:57,050
Hello, beautiful.

1140
01:58:02,350 --> 01:58:05,360
Well, don't hang about. Snatch 'em.

1141
01:59:17,680 --> 01:59:20,750
Harry. Tell me what to do.

1142
01:59:20,750 --> 01:59:22,190
Tell me, where it is.

1143
01:59:23,290 --> 01:59:25,940
Grindelwald. Grindelwald.

1144
01:59:28,910 --> 01:59:31,070
I knew you'd come, one day.

1145
01:59:31,590 --> 01:59:32,940
But surely you must know.

1146
01:59:32,940 --> 01:59:35,140
I no longer have what you seek.

1147
01:59:35,740 --> 01:59:38,350
Tell me, Grindelwald, tell me where it is.

1148
01:59:38,650 --> 01:59:40,410
Tell me who possesses it.

1149
01:59:40,810 --> 01:59:45,530
The elder wand lies with him, of course.

1150
01:59:46,090 --> 01:59:47,750
Buried in the earth.

1151
01:59:49,170 --> 01:59:50,450
Dumbledore.

1152
02:00:00,070 --> 02:00:01,390
The Hallows exist.

1153
02:00:01,770 --> 02:00:03,380
But he's only after one of them, the last one.

1154
02:00:03,550 --> 02:00:04,810
He knows where it is.

1155
02:00:05,620 --> 02:00:06,920
He's gonna have it by the end of the night.

1156
02:00:06,920 --> 02:00:08,380
You know who's had the elder wand?

1157
02:00:09,790 --> 02:00:12,040
- Don't touch her! - Leave him.

1158
02:00:12,080 --> 02:00:15,060
Your boyfriend will get much worse

1159
02:00:15,060 --> 02:00:18,550
than that if he doesn't learn to behave himself.

1160
02:00:20,890 --> 02:00:22,380
What happened to you, ugly?

1161
02:00:24,070 --> 02:00:25,270
No, not you.

1162
02:00:27,370 --> 02:00:30,560
- What's your name? - Dudley. Vernon Dudley.

1163
02:00:30,750 --> 02:00:31,660
Check it.

1164
02:00:34,490 --> 02:00:36,780
And you, my lovely.

1165
02:00:39,870 --> 02:00:41,020
What do they call you?

1166
02:00:43,440 --> 02:00:46,830
Penelope Clearwater, half-blood.

1167
02:00:50,830 --> 02:00:52,350
There's no Vernon Dudley on here.

1168
02:00:53,610 --> 02:00:56,210
You hear that ugly? This says you're lying.

1169
02:00:57,250 --> 02:00:59,450
How come you don't want us to know who you are?

1170
02:00:59,450 --> 02:01:01,640
It's wrong, I told you who I am.

1171
02:01:18,340 --> 02:01:19,460
Change of plan.

1172
02:01:21,630 --> 02:01:23,870
We're not taking this lot to the Ministry.

1173
02:02:04,490 --> 02:02:07,100
Get, Draco.

1174
02:02:12,680 --> 02:02:13,630
Well?

1175
02:02:17,440 --> 02:02:18,380
I can't be sure.

1176
02:02:19,720 --> 02:02:21,030
Look closely, son.

1177
02:02:22,790 --> 02:02:26,950
If we are the ones to hand Potter over to the Dark Lord.

1178
02:02:28,080 --> 02:02:29,790
Everything would be forgiven,

1179
02:02:29,790 --> 02:02:32,840
it would be as it was, understand?

1180
02:02:33,460 --> 02:02:35,790
Now we won't be forgetting who really actually caught him.

1181
02:02:36,210 --> 02:02:38,170
I hope, Mr. Malfoy.

1182
02:02:38,170 --> 02:02:41,330
- You dare to talk to me like that in my own house! - Lucius!

1183
02:02:45,080 --> 02:02:47,930
Do not be shy, sweetie. Come closer.

1184
02:02:50,210 --> 02:02:51,860
Now, if this isn't who you think it is, Draco,

1185
02:02:51,900 --> 02:02:55,690
and we call Him. He'll kill us all.

1186
02:02:55,690 --> 02:02:57,260
We need to be absolutely sure.

1187
02:02:58,570 --> 02:03:01,240
- What's wrong with his face? - Yes, what is wrong with his face?

1188
02:03:01,280 --> 02:03:02,900
He came to us like that.

1189
02:03:02,900 --> 02:03:05,730
Something he picked up in the forest, I reckon.

1190
02:03:05,810 --> 02:03:08,530
An interesting jinx. Was it you, dear?

1191
02:03:13,440 --> 02:03:14,670
Give me her wand,

1192
02:03:14,670 --> 02:03:16,460
let's see what your last spell was.

1193
02:03:19,320 --> 02:03:19,860
Got you.

1194
02:03:23,990 --> 02:03:25,110
What's that?

1195
02:03:27,480 --> 02:03:28,760
Where'd you get that from?

1196
02:03:28,890 --> 02:03:30,540
It was in her bag when we searched her.

1197
02:03:31,460 --> 02:03:32,530
I reckon it's mine now.

1198
02:03:36,370 --> 02:03:37,450
Are you mad?

1199
02:03:46,210 --> 02:03:48,220
Get out! Get out!

1200
02:03:56,260 --> 02:03:58,490
Cissy, put the boys in the cellar.

1201
02:03:58,920 --> 02:04:01,600
I want a conversation with this one.

1202
02:04:01,980 --> 02:04:03,520
Girl to girl!

1203
02:04:13,490 --> 02:04:14,110
What are we gonna do?

1204
02:04:14,110 --> 02:04:15,670
We can't leave Hermione alone with her.

1205
02:04:16,700 --> 02:04:17,500
Ron?

1206
02:04:23,220 --> 02:04:24,000
Harry?

1207
02:04:30,340 --> 02:04:31,460
Luna?

1208
02:04:32,510 --> 02:04:35,550
That Sword is meant to be in my vault now,

1209
02:04:35,550 --> 02:04:36,970
how did you get it?

1210
02:04:37,420 --> 02:04:42,230
Did you and your friend's take it from my vault?

1211
02:04:42,460 --> 02:04:45,680
I didn't take anything!

1212
02:04:45,900 --> 02:04:47,100
I don't believe you.

1213
02:04:52,910 --> 02:04:55,370
- We have to do something! - There is no way out of here.

1214
02:04:55,370 --> 02:04:58,760
We tried everything. It's enchanted.

1215
02:05:01,330 --> 02:05:02,420
You're bleeding, Harry.

1216
02:05:02,420 --> 02:05:05,510
That's a curious thing to keep on yourself.

1217
02:05:14,700 --> 02:05:15,720
Help us!

1218
02:05:21,490 --> 02:05:23,640
- Let her go. - You go, get back!

1219
02:05:24,750 --> 02:05:28,120
You, Goblin. Come with me.

1220
02:05:48,840 --> 02:05:52,020
Dobby? What are you doing here?

1221
02:05:52,070 --> 02:05:54,630
Dobby's come to rescue, Harry Potter of course.

1222
02:05:54,880 --> 02:05:57,350
Dobby will always be there for Harry Potter.

1223
02:05:57,350 --> 02:05:59,580
Are you saying that you can apparate in and out of this room?

1224
02:05:59,910 --> 02:06:01,220
Could you take us with you?

1225
02:06:01,220 --> 02:06:02,900
Of course, sir, I'm a elf.

1226
02:06:03,760 --> 02:06:04,940
Works for me.

1227
02:06:06,030 --> 02:06:07,770
Right, Dobby, I want you to take Luna and Mr. Ollivander...

1228
02:06:08,010 --> 02:06:09,940
Shell Cottage, on the outskirts of Tinworth.

1229
02:06:11,470 --> 02:06:12,400
Trust me.

1230
02:06:13,260 --> 02:06:14,680
When ever you're ready, sir.

1231
02:06:15,220 --> 02:06:17,790
Sir? I like her very much!

1232
02:06:22,520 --> 02:06:25,550
Meet me at top of the stairs in ten seconds.

1233
02:06:42,490 --> 02:06:44,000
Who gets his wand?

1234
02:06:48,510 --> 02:06:51,660
I'm going to ask you once more, goblin.

1235
02:06:51,730 --> 02:06:54,320
Think very, very carefully.

1236
02:06:54,340 --> 02:06:56,050
- How did they get there? - I don't know.

1237
02:06:57,090 --> 02:07:00,540
You don't know? Why were you doing your job?

1238
02:07:00,620 --> 02:07:03,000
Who got into my vault?

1239
02:07:05,020 --> 02:07:06,180
Who stole it?

1240
02:07:06,330 --> 02:07:08,300
Who... Stole it?

1241
02:07:09,940 --> 02:07:13,090
It's impossible to break into Gringotts, the sword is there.

1242
02:07:17,030 --> 02:07:20,230
Then how is it that it's out then?

1243
02:07:20,300 --> 02:07:22,660
There is no place safer, than Gringotts.

1244
02:07:22,660 --> 02:07:23,490
Liar!

1245
02:07:25,470 --> 02:07:28,020
Consider yourself lucky, goblin.

1246
02:07:31,750 --> 02:07:36,030
- The same won't be said for this one. - Like hell!

1247
02:07:37,340 --> 02:07:38,480
Expelliarmus.

1248
02:07:40,270 --> 02:07:41,290
Stupefy!

1249
02:07:45,110 --> 02:07:46,110
Stop!

1250
02:07:48,150 --> 02:07:49,290
Drop your wands.

1251
02:07:52,710 --> 02:07:53,880
I said, drop them!

1252
02:07:55,560 --> 02:07:58,730
Pick 'em up, Draco, now! Well, well, well.

1253
02:07:59,100 --> 02:08:00,820
Look what we have here.

1254
02:08:03,260 --> 02:08:04,390
It's Harry Potter.

1255
02:08:05,500 --> 02:08:08,190
He's all bright, shiny and new again.

1256
02:08:08,700 --> 02:08:11,590
Just in time for the Dark Lord.

1257
02:08:11,830 --> 02:08:13,090
Call him.

1258
02:08:17,740 --> 02:08:18,590
Call him.

1259
02:08:54,430 --> 02:08:55,800
Stupefy!

1260
02:08:57,530 --> 02:09:00,350
Stupid elf! You could have kill me!

1261
02:09:00,350 --> 02:09:02,280
Dobby never meant to kill.

1262
02:09:02,400 --> 02:09:06,460
Dobby only meant to maim or seriously injure.

1263
02:09:09,240 --> 02:09:11,940
How dare you take a witch's wand.

1264
02:09:12,260 --> 02:09:14,990
How dare you defy your masters.

1265
02:09:15,390 --> 02:09:18,460
Dobby has no master.

1266
02:09:18,630 --> 02:09:21,340
Dobby is a free elf.

1267
02:09:21,390 --> 02:09:25,640
And Dobby has come to save Harry Potter and his friends.

1268
02:09:55,940 --> 02:09:58,930
Hermione, are you all right?

1269
02:09:59,060 --> 02:10:01,830
We're safe. We're all safe.

1270
02:10:03,670 --> 02:10:04,820
Harry Potter...

1271
02:10:09,660 --> 02:10:10,450
Dobby!

1272
02:10:21,980 --> 02:10:24,230
Dobby, you're all right then, hold on.

1273
02:10:25,190 --> 02:10:26,120
Hold on, okay?

1274
02:10:27,700 --> 02:10:30,940
Just hold on, okay? We're going to fix it.

1275
02:10:32,310 --> 02:10:34,120
Hermione, you have something...

1276
02:10:35,030 --> 02:10:37,660
In your bag. Hermione!

1277
02:10:38,700 --> 02:10:39,550
Come on.

1278
02:10:43,610 --> 02:10:44,330
Help me.

1279
02:10:48,250 --> 02:10:50,540
Such a beautiful place,

1280
02:10:53,190 --> 02:10:55,470
to be with friends.

1281
02:10:57,410 --> 02:10:58,670
Dobby is happy,

1282
02:11:00,690 --> 02:11:03,320
to be with be with his friend,

1283
02:11:05,540 --> 02:11:07,000
Harry Potter.

1284
02:11:28,270 --> 02:11:30,260
We should close his eyes.

1285
02:11:31,340 --> 02:11:32,420
Don't you think?

1286
02:11:39,380 --> 02:11:41,740
There, now he could be sleeping.

1287
02:11:58,030 --> 02:11:59,180
I want to bury him.

1288
02:12:00,900 --> 02:12:03,800
Properly, without magic.

